Code adapted from other projects
--------------------------------
- The System One scorer (accuracy, KL from gold, Brier, ECE) follows
  bench/score_with_jobs.py of LocalLLaMA/typed-decisions (Apache-2.0). The typed question
  shape (choice, score, noul) follows the TypeSafe System One API as served by llama.cpp's
  /v1/systemone. LvW-bench is not affiliated with TypeSafe, LocalLLaMA or Liquid AI.
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/LocalLLaMA/typed-decisions
- The IFEval checks in internal/score/ifeval.go, web/js/score.js and bench/score.py are
  rewritten from google-research/instruction_following_eval (Apache-2.0), for the
  instructions listed there. Keywords are matched literally.
  https://github.com/google-research/google-research/tree/master/instruction_following_eval
- The spot_snake workflow reproduces the text format and teacher of
  Lucasgitguy-co/spot-snake-decisions-v0.1 and github.com/Gitguy268/spot-snake (MIT).

Runtime dependencies (not included in the data)
-----------------------------------------------
- Go: charmbracelet/bubbletea, bubbles, lipgloss (MIT); wailsapp/wails v2 (MIT) for the app.
- llama.cpp (MIT) is called as a separate program (llama-server); it is not bundled.
- Python helper: PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause), transformers, accelerate, peft, huggingface_hub
  (Apache-2.0), safetensors (Apache-2.0), sentence-transformers (Apache-2.0). Installed by
  uv at run time, not bundled.
- Browser runner: wllama (MIT), WebLLM (Apache-2.0), loaded from a CDN at run time.

Ideas, no code
--------------
- TPN Workbench (bench.trueperformancenetwork.com): results tied to the exact weights,
  safetensors and GGUF inputs, rotating private sets (here: the seeded generated set).
- EleutherAI lm-evaluation-harness: task selection. Scoring here is on generated answers,
  so scores are not comparable with lm-eval loglikelihood numbers.

Models are not part of LvW-bench. Each model keeps its own licence (for example the Spot
Snake d1 models are LvW-license-Snake-1.0, derived from the LFM Open License v1.0).
